      'Include replacement part SKUs and warranty handling for damaged freight. Retail buyers forward those details to operations; missing them triggers a second sales cycle you could have avoided. Clarify sample policies: cost, credit-back rules, and how many days samples stay out. Sample ambiguity slows openings more than price disagreements in many categories, especially when merchandisers need a physical read before committing shelf space.',
      'Map which claims are approved for retailer circulars versus brand site only. Buyers who paste direct-to-consumer lifestyle lines into circulars can create compliance problems you will own relationally even if the legal picture is nuanced. Offer a short competitive contrast section grounded in measurable specs, not insults. Purchasing committees compare matrices; help them do it with your numbers rather than forcing them to retype from scattered PDFs.',
