      'Score opening paragraphs on sentence length and jargon density. Count words over three syllables that are not necessary product terms. Prestige vocabulary that needs a glossary fails paid audiences who arrived mid-scroll from a short video. Check promise continuity from ad creative to headline. If the ad features “silent for apartments,” that claim must appear near the fold, not in a buried FAQ. Discontinuity produces bounces that look like bad targeting in the ad platform when the landing page is the culprit.',
      'Verify scannability: bullets with concrete attributes, subheads that name decisions, and whitespace that separates modules. Walls of supplier prose kill paid traffic faster than organic browsers, because paid visitors are less patient and more comparison-prone. Time a stranger to find the shipping promise and the return window. If either takes more than fifteen seconds, elevate those lines. Clarity of logistics often decides conversion after the product itself is understood.',
