      'For made-to-order art or furniture, include production stage markers such as queued, in finish, and in quality assurance on the order page. Visible progress reduces where-is-my-order volume without overpromising dates. Disallow gift messaging that implies arrival by a hard personal date unless fulfillment can commit. “Arrives before her birthday” copy on a preorder SKU is how brands inherit emotional deadlines they cannot meet and then inherit the public anger that follows.',
