      'Maintain a master fact sheet per SKU: title backbone, bullet facts, long-description facts, care, warnings, weight with packaging, and contents of the box. Every channel draft pulls from that sheet. Voice may change for handmade storytelling versus marketplace bullets; wattage, fiber content, and accessory counts may not. Treat any channel-only "enhancement" of specs as a data incident.',
      'Channel formatting rules differ in ways that tempt writers to invent. Marketplaces reward scannable bullets and punish promotional language in certain fields. Handmade marketplaces favor process and maker story. Your own storefront lets you blend brand narrative with modules. Map which facts land in which field types so writers stop reinventing structure mid-flow and accidentally adding a feature only Amazon shoppers see.',
      'Banned-claim lists should be global. If a marketplace will not allow a health claim, you also should not feature it on your storefront just because the theme looks prettier. Divergent claims get screenshotted side by side by sophisticated buyers, disgruntled affiliates, and regulators. One truth set is cheaper than three cleanup projects.',
