      'Pricing and promotion honesty matters even when algorithms encourage games. Large unexplained gaps invite showrooming anger and public complaints. If a marketplace price is lower because of fulfillment economics, keep the product promise identical and let price be the only intentional difference. Do not compensate for a higher DTC price by inventing exclusive features that are not exclusive.',
      'Imagery sets should share the hero truth while adapting to channel constraints such as white-background requirements versus lifestyle-friendly thumbnails. Never show a gift-wrap upgrade on one channel\'s main image if that upgrade is unavailable elsewhere without disclosure. Props, extras, and in-box accessories must match the shared contents list or be labeled optional everywhere they appear.',
      'Review feedback loops must update all channels. A safety clarification added to your storefront after an incident needs marketplace updates in the same sprint. Single-channel patches are how contradictory care instructions spread, and how a customer who bought on one site follows care advice from another and damages the product.',
      'Assign a channel steward and a fact owner as different roles when volume grows. The steward knows field limits, keyword norms, and policy traps. The fact owner approves scientific or compliance language. Conflating the roles produces either slow listings that miss launches or creative facts that ship before anyone with measurement tools looked twice.',
      'When rewriting dozens of SKUs for a relaunch, work from the master sheet outward—channel templates second. Bulk rewrites that start from the messiest marketplace scrape tend to proliferate errors across every storefront at once. Clean center, then radiate. If you need speed across many SKUs, rewrite from the sheet in bulk, then spot-check channel outputs for field truncation that silently dropped a warning.',
      'Audit quarterly: pick twenty SKUs at random, open all three storefronts, and score mismatches on a simple rubric covering facts, titles, images, and policies. Publish the mismatch count internally; visibility drives fixes more than a forgotten style PDF. Celebrate reductions the same way you celebrate conversion wins, because consistency is a conversion and CX feature.',
      'Syndication tools help but do not forgive bad source data. Garbage in remains garbage on three platforms with better distribution. Invest in sheet quality, naming discipline, and claim governance before celebrating automation dashboards that simply scale your contradictions faster than a human team ever could.',
      'Shoppers reward brands that feel like one company everywhere they look. Operationally that feeling is boring discipline: same millimeters, same inclusions, same warnings, dressed in each marketplace\'s costume without changing the character underneath. Cross-channel trust is slow to build and quick to lose when one listing oversells what another listing carefully disclosed.',
      'When a channel forces shorter copy, cut color and story first, never safety, contents, or dimensions. A truncated aesthetic paragraph is recoverable; a truncated allergen line is not. Train freelancers on that priority order explicitly, because left to taste they will keep the pretty sentence and drop the inconvenient constraint that prevents chargebacks.',
      'Handle exclusive channel bundles carefully. If Amazon receives a value pack your DTC site does not sell, create a distinct SKU identity and fact sheet rather than overloading the base product\'s shared sheet with optional extras. Confused exclusivity is still a consistency failure when customers believe every channel ships the same contents.',
