      'Progressive disclosure in layout often beats an all-or-nothing word-count argument. Above the fold: identity, primary benefit, and top specs. Below: story, comparisons, and deeper care. Mobile shoppers get speed; careful researchers get depth without a separate blog post that severs context from the buy button and loses attribution.',
      'Variants change the math. Shared descriptions across colors should stay moderate while finish-specific notes under each swatch explain how olive versus charcoal reads indoors. A long shared essay that never mentions finish leaves half your buyers guessing — and guessing is how return carts fill with items that were never wrong, only misunderstood.',
      'SEO pressure should not manufacture fake length. Search systems reward useful uniqueness, not synonym padding. A genuine FAQ answering a compatibility question beats ornamental adjectives every time. If you need more indexable text, add true answers shoppers search for, not decorative paragraphs that say nothing a competitor could not copy.',
