      'Legal categories such as supplements, children\'s products, and regulated electronics require disclosures that expand length whether marketers prefer scannability or not. Design those mandated sections as scannable lists so compliance text does not drown benefits. The goal is not maximal brevity; it is maximal clarity per pixel the shopper is willing to give you before deciding.',
      'Bundled kits often need a medium hybrid: a short overview naming the set purpose, then longer line-item blurbs for each component. Dumping one giant essay that never inventories pieces leaves shoppers unsure what arrives. Length follows assembly of understanding, not an aesthetic preference for short or long alone.',
